  {
   "id": 666555,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the output?<br>\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">def update_hour():\n&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour = hour\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if is_dst:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour += 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;else:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour -= 1\n\nis_dst = True\nhour = int(input(\"Enter hour: \"))\nupdate_hour()\nprint(\"New hour:\", new_hour)\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328718,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 9</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "hour has the value 9 but is not being printed. new_hour has the value 10 but is out of scope in the print statement."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328719,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 10</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "new_hour has the value of 10 in update_hour(), but the value is discarded after update_hour() finishes. new_hour is out of scope in the print statement."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328720,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Error</code>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">new_hour</code> is a local variable that the print statement tries to access after <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">update_hour()</code> finishes. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">new_hour</code> is out of scope, so an error is produced."
    }
   ],
